  "notes": "The one bright-mode entry on this axis. The research says the early bubblegum records sit in major and Lydian-tinged bright modes — rare in trap — so `session.keys` is authored with major spellings and `scales` is weighted toward major/lydian, and the chord families carry I–IV–vi and I–V–vi alongside the minor pair the later rap records use. Melody is the childlike-diatonic parameter set: the highest `chordToneBias` and the lowest `halfStepDissonance` in this batch, step-dominant intervals, and a `music_box_pluck` timbre for the chiptune/music-box palette the research names. Drums are the light end — simple kick placement, 16th hats, light rolls. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ The 808 is the INFERRED parameter: the research describes two opposite 808s (short and clean on the bright material, long and distorted with glides on the later Michigan/ATL-hybrid cuts) and this model splits the difference at `distortion: medium` with `glideProb` 0.3 rather than authoring modes, because the research gives no weighting between the two lanes. ⚠ The beat switches and half-length interludes the research names are not authored — the arrangement vocabulary has no section-length-halving device. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
